#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "Who made this game?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The kdegames team. You can find their website <ulink url=\"http://games.kde."
"org\">here</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where can I get cheatcodes?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid "You cannot get cheatcodes for &kde; games."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I start a new game?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can start a new game using the <guibutton>New</guibutton> button on the "
"toolbar, the <menuchoice><guimenu>Game</guimenu><guimenuitem>New</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu entry on the menubar or using the default "
"shortcut <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>N</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I pause the game?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kjumpingcube; does not have a <quote>Pause</quote> feature, as none is "
"required."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid "I want to change the way this game looks. Can I?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Currently you can only change the player's colors, but not the game theme. "
"To change the player's colors use the <link linkend=\"configuration\">Game "
"Configuration</link> dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid "I have made a mistake. Can I undo?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. To undo your last move you can use a <link linkend=\"move-menu-undo"
"\">menubar option</link>, or a <link linkend=\"move-menu-undo\">keyboard "
"shortcut</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I use keyboard?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "No. &kjumpingcube; cannot be played using the keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid "I cannot figure out what to do here! Are there hints?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. To see a hint you can use a <link linkend=\"move-menu-hint\">menubar "
"option</link>, or a <link linkend=\"move-menu-hint\">keyboard shortcut</"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I have to quit the game now, but I am not finished yet. Can I save my "
"position?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. To save your position use a <link linkend=\"menu-game-save"
"\"><guimenuitem>Save</guimenuitem> option</link> on the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I restore the game I saved?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To load your position in a saved game use the <link linkend=\"menu-game-load"
"\"><guimenuitem>Load...</guimenuitem> option</link> on the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where are the high scores?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kjumpingcube; does not have such a feature."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid "I want to change the game configuration. Where do I go?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The game <link linkend=\"configuration\">configuration dialog</link> can be "
"invoked using <link linkend=\"settings-menu-configure"
"\"><guimenuitem>Configure &kjumpingcube;...</guimenuitem> option</link> on "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid "I want to change the toolbar layout. What do I do?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the toolbar layout use the <link linkend=\"settings-menu-toolbar"
"\"><guimenuitem>Configure Toolbars...</guimenuitem> option</link> on the "
"menubar."
msgstr ""

